In theory, yes, AFAIK.  I've heard that you may stash a bag of holding
in a sack, and continue putting that sack into another sack, recursively.
Finally, after seven or so sacks, you may put the sack into another bag
of holding with no (or at least reduced) risk of exploding.  Thus you
may dramatically increase your carrying capacity.  (Might help to get a
great highscore?)

Another usage for more than one bag is if you play careless (like I
sometimes happen to do), drop the bag and let it be eaten.

Or something else that happened to me: my strong pet picked it up and
the pet and the bag got disintegrated by a black dragon.

Ignoring these three cases (and maybe indefinitely more cases I can not
think of), three bags of holdings are as good as one bag of holding if
you put one bag into the next bag <oops> into the last bag. (Says the
oracle ambiguously as always.)

